//// Decision 55 — `break <value>` in a collection loop **contributes its value
//// and ends the loop**. Decided 2026-09-18; written into decision 8 §10.
////
//// `yield` first, then a conditional value `break`: 10 yields 20, 20 yields 40
//// and then breaks with 99, and 30 is never visited. So the loop is
//// `[20, 40, 99]` — three elements.
////
//// Measured at `b5a9b85d`, no backend gives it:
////
////   commonJS  3  20,40,60      — the break value is dropped and the loop runs on
////   beam      3  20,40,60      — the same
////   erlang    3  ok,99,ok      — the yielded values are lost; every non-breaking
////                               iteration answers the `ok` of its last statement
////   wasm      4  20,40,99,60   — the break value is appended and the loop runs on
////
//// Re-measured at `85f883bd` (2026-09-20), after C-06's wasm half (`8594e4ba`): wasm
//// answers `3` / `20,40,99` and its line is gone; the other three are unchanged.
////
//// The result is read as `length` + `join(",")` rather than printed as an array
//// so that §7's separator row cannot hide this one.

pub fn main() {
    val r = for ([10, 20, 30]) { x ->
        yield x * 2;
        if (x == 20) { break 99; };
    };
    @print(r.length);
    @print(r.join(","));
}
